Normative changes between the two pins, read from the files above:

(a) `ModelNode.semantic_form` (schema.json) drops the three-form list
`model_import`/`model_type`/`model_declaration` and replaces it with FR-208's
eighteen meanings: `model_import`, `object_type`, `value_type`, `variant_type`,
`record_value_type`, `event_type`, `state_machine`, `process`,
`persistence_interface`, `namespace`, `field_declaration`,
`operation_declaration`, `clause_member_declaration`, `systems_interface`,
`systems_part`, `systems_port`, `systems_connection` and `systems_allocation`.
`model_type` and `model_declaration` are deleted upstream, not retained
alongside the new forms.

(b) `FrameBody` (schema.json) is a new closed shape,
`{term: "frame", modifies, creates, deletes}` (each a `NodeRef` array),
selected in place of the ordinary `SemanticTerm` grammar by
`BodyBindingRules` for exactly a `state` node with `semantic_form: "frame"`
(FR-340). Eligibility of each entry against the meaning of the dependency it
names, canonical member order, and refusal precedence among a frame's own
violations are FR-340/FR-013 obligations this vendor's reader does not
enforce; see the reader-scope note below.

(c) The `Declaration` member (schema.json, FR-322, FR-208) is a new closed
shape `{qualified_name}` carried by a named, source-declared
`scalar_type`/`composite_type`/`bounded_domain`/`function`/`model`/`protocol`/
`claim` node or a non-`enum_value` `value` node, exactly when the node has a
`declaration` source occurrence (`DeclarationOccurrenceRule`); it is forbidden
on `expression`, `relation`, `state`, `temporal`, `correspondence` and
`enum_value` nodes (`DeclarationTagRules`).

(d) `literal.type` and `application.operation`/`application.result_type`
(schema.json) are new required members: a `literal` term now carries its
declared `type` (a node reference) beside `value_kind`/`value`, and an
`application` term now carries a catalogued `operation` identity
(`{identity, laws, mode, member, leaves}`) and a declared `result_type` (a
node reference) beside `operator`/`arguments`. Neither type is inferred. The
new `Operation`/`OperationIdentity`/`OperationLaw`/`OperationMode`/
`OperationMember`/`OperationLeaf` family (schema.json, and
`operation-catalog.json`'s `quire.checked-operation-catalog/v1` entries) gives
`operation`'s closed shape; this vendor's reader admits the member opaquely
(present, well-formed JSON) and validates only `result_type` as a reference.
The operation catalog's own eligibility, law/mode/member/leaf matching, and
the refusal family FR-322 defines for it are not implemented here.

(e) `ExpressionNode.semantic_form` (schema.json) gains two forms in the
otherwise-unchanged list: `collection` and `value_read`.

(f) `PackageId`'s constituent `package_selections` are unaffected, but every
`package_id` and node id computed over a graph that uses any of (a)-(e)
changes, because `identity_projection` includes `declaration` and the new
required `literal`/`application` members; `positive-all-families.json`,
`positive-nominal-identities.json`, `positive-clause-operations.json`,
`positive-control-operations.json` and `positive-operation-identities.json`
all re-derive their `package_id`s at this pin, verified in
`positive-nominal-identities.json`, whose node 1's `declaration` gains
`{"qualified_name": ["Example", "Status"]}` and whose node 0's `body` gains a
`type` reference to node 1.

(g) `node-identity-vectors.json` gains three new top-level vector arrays
alongside the unchanged `vectors` (14 entries) and `invalid_mutations` (12
entries): `frame_mutations` (26 entries, one of them,
`cross-frame-lower-digest-wins`, carrying a complete inline `second_frame`
node), `operation_vectors` (21 entries) and `operation_mutations` (24
entries), verified by loading the vendored file and counting each array.

(h) FR-322's refusal code vocabulary grows from 11 to 16 members: it gains
`invalid_package`, `ill_typed` and `ambiguous_declaration` (operation and
declaration causes) and, at this pin, `missing_declaration` and
`invalid_model_binding` (frame-entry causes FR-340 defines). FR-322 and
interface_004 also now state the reader's cause-carrying refusal order
normatively: graph-shape, then `stale-node-key`, then declaration
(`declaration-nominal-mismatch`/`ambiguous-name`), then frame
(FR-340's own meaning-join/canonical-order precedence, at the first
`state`/`frame` node in ascending node-id digest order with a defect), then
operation. This vendor's reader implements none of the ordering beyond
graph-shape and declaration; it carries none of the five cause-carrying codes
and enforces frame bodies only for shape and `uniqueItems`, not for meaning-
join, order or precedence.

Reader scope at this pin: this reader admits every new wire member (b)-(e)
above structurally and enforces (c)'s two binding rules exactly. For (b) it
recognizes only the `frame` shape's own closed member set, its `uniqueItems`
constraint, and reference arrays; it does not check an entry's eligibility
against the meaning of the node it names, does not enforce canonical member
order, and does not implement FR-340/FR-013's refusal precedence among a
frame's own violations. For (d) it does not implement the operation catalog,
its law/mode/member/leaf matching, or the refusal family and ordering (h)
describes. Frame and operation semantics are a later change's scope.

